WEBVTT

00:00:00.470 --> 00:00:02.140
Stop!

00:00:02.140 --> 00:00:04.350
Stop! Stop!

00:00:04.790 --> 00:00:05.980
Which way did it go?!

00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:07.240
Which way?! Which way?!

00:00:07.690 --> 00:00:08.920
This way?!

00:00:08.920 --> 00:00:10.080
This way?

00:00:10.640 --> 00:00:11.990
Down here!

00:00:11.990 --> 00:00:13.240
Down here?

00:00:14.540 --> 00:00:16.010
Where did it go?!

00:00:16.010 --> 00:00:17.630
Where, where?

00:00:17.630 --> 00:00:19.670
It's noisy for some reason.

00:00:20.260 --> 00:00:21.260
In here?!

00:00:28.280 --> 00:00:29.210
Who're you?

00:00:30.320 --> 00:00:31.470
Rindou?!

00:00:31.470 --> 00:00:33.680
I've never seen your face!

00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:35.190
You're cute.

00:00:35.550 --> 00:00:37.240
You took off your mask?

00:00:37.240 --> 00:00:37.990
Yeah.

00:00:37.990 --> 00:00:39.150
Wow!

00:00:39.150 --> 00:00:42.820
What were you three chasing?

00:00:42.820 --> 00:00:44.450
Oh, that's right.

00:00:44.450 --> 00:00:46.440
Hey, did you see a snake?

00:00:46.440 --> 00:00:47.360
A snake?

00:00:47.360 --> 00:00:48.860
One of Sensei's snakes!

00:00:49.150 --> 00:00:51.610
It was written on the signpost outside.

00:00:51.610 --> 00:00:53.690
<b>Whoever catches
 my snakes by lunchtime 
gets more rice and side dishes
- Hana</b>

00:00:52.220 --> 00:00:57.290
It said if you catch one by lunchtime, 
your team gets extra side dishes!

00:00:57.290 --> 00:01:00.530
Oh, that's why you were running around.

00:01:00.530 --> 00:01:01.690
Yeah.

00:01:01.690 --> 00:01:04.340
Asagao and Sazanka saw one, too.

00:01:07.610 --> 00:01:09.410
Snake!

00:01:09.410 --> 00:01:12.180
I can't move. Calm down.

00:01:15.020 --> 00:01:16.860
So, this is one of them.

00:01:17.340 --> 00:01:19.730
<b>Tofu</b>

00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:19.730
"Tofu"?

00:01:19.730 --> 00:01:22.590
Oh, that's the one we were after!

00:01:22.590 --> 00:01:24.490
Ahh, I get it.

00:01:24.710 --> 00:01:27.170
The side dish you get more 
of is written on them.

00:01:30.700 --> 00:01:32.500
Here you go.

00:01:35.250 --> 00:01:37.140
I-In here.

00:01:37.140 --> 00:01:38.500
Hooray!

00:01:41.950 --> 00:01:44.160
Yay! Tofu! Tofu!

00:01:44.160 --> 00:01:45.380
Thanks!

00:01:45.380 --> 00:01:47.080
See ya!

00:01:47.080 --> 00:01:48.110
We owe you one.

00:01:50.520 --> 00:01:51.820
Yes!

00:01:56.240 --> 00:01:59.830
Why don't we go snake hunting, too?

00:01:59.830 --> 00:02:00.480
Sure.

00:03:32.020 --> 00:03:33.440
Side dishes, huh?

00:03:32.020 --> 00:03:35.560
<b>Of Snakes and Men</b>

00:03:33.440 --> 00:03:35.810
I want some pickled veggies.

00:03:35.810 --> 00:03:37.410
That sounds good.

00:03:37.410 --> 00:03:39.100
What do you like, Tsubaki?

00:03:39.100 --> 00:03:42.420
Let's see... What I like is—

00:03:42.420 --> 00:03:44.980
A man! It went that way!

00:03:44.980 --> 00:03:45.530
Huh?!

00:03:49.600 --> 00:03:51.300
Tsubaki, are you okay?

00:03:51.300 --> 00:03:54.640
It's rare to see Tsubaki fall from a tree.

00:03:54.640 --> 00:03:56.590
Wh-Where's the man?!

00:03:57.880 --> 00:03:59.800
Oh, you mean that.

00:03:59.800 --> 00:04:01.850
Hold it, you man!

00:04:01.850 --> 00:04:03.300
You man!

00:04:03.300 --> 00:04:05.300
Get back here!

00:04:05.860 --> 00:04:08.100
That's what they're calling the snake.

00:04:05.860 --> 00:04:08.100
You man!

00:04:08.100 --> 00:04:09.640
You man!

00:04:09.930 --> 00:04:13.700
Snakes are creepy, so the thinking is,

00:04:13.700 --> 00:04:16.720
maybe you'll feel more like 
catching one if you call it a man.

00:04:18.140 --> 00:04:19.570
Bad girls!

00:04:19.570 --> 00:04:22.660
Playing around by making light of men again!

00:04:22.660 --> 00:04:24.580
Sensei's going to be mad!

00:04:24.580 --> 00:04:27.140
I'm not the one who came up with it.

00:04:27.140 --> 00:04:28.840
Then, who did?!

00:04:30.490 --> 00:04:32.360
Sazanka and Asagao.

00:04:34.560 --> 00:04:35.800
There it goes!

00:04:35.800 --> 00:04:36.540
That way!

00:04:41.340 --> 00:04:43.340
Isn't it, like, way fast?

00:04:43.340 --> 00:04:44.970
Take a look at the writing.

00:04:45.570 --> 00:04:46.760
Writing?

00:04:46.760 --> 00:04:49.100
<b>Meat</b>

00:04:47.440 --> 00:04:49.100
Oh! Meat!

00:04:49.540 --> 00:04:51.810
Higher difficulty, for a good catch.

00:04:51.810 --> 00:04:54.020
I'm motivated now!

00:04:54.320 --> 00:04:58.110
Yeah! If we catch it, I can 
get Nee-sama to praise me!

00:04:58.110 --> 00:04:59.320
Sazanka!

00:05:00.910 --> 00:05:02.570
Oh! Nee-sama!

00:05:02.570 --> 00:05:06.740
Good timing! Catch that, Tsubaki-chan!

00:05:07.980 --> 00:05:09.860
We might as well catch it.

00:05:09.860 --> 00:05:10.550
Yeah.

00:05:11.580 --> 00:05:12.560
My mask—

00:05:20.510 --> 00:05:21.800
My meat!

00:05:21.800 --> 00:05:25.010
Sorry. My mask's string 
has been loose lately.

00:05:25.220 --> 00:05:29.140
Darn it! That was the meat man!

00:05:29.140 --> 00:05:30.510
"Man"?

00:05:31.070 --> 00:05:35.520
I have something to say to 
you two, regarding that.

00:05:35.520 --> 00:05:36.920
But, the meat...

00:05:36.920 --> 00:05:38.310
Never mind that.

00:05:38.540 --> 00:05:40.220
Sit your butts down!

00:05:40.220 --> 00:05:41.680
Yes, ma'am!

00:05:44.410 --> 00:05:49.960
How many times have I told you not 
to play around by making fun of men?!

00:05:49.960 --> 00:05:54.700
I swear, no matter how many times 
I say it, you two never learn!

00:05:54.700 --> 00:05:57.000
You hear me? You learned 
this in class too, right?

00:05:57.000 --> 00:05:59.330
Men are horrible! Things to be feared!

00:05:59.330 --> 00:06:02.050
Can you please explain to me 
how it is that everything,

00:06:02.050 --> 00:06:06.060
<i>every</i> single thing you learn in class 
goes in one ear and out the other...

00:06:09.550 --> 00:06:12.720
And so, be more careful from now on.

00:06:12.720 --> 00:06:13.820
Understood?

00:06:13.820 --> 00:06:14.800
Yes, ma'am.

00:06:14.800 --> 00:06:16.530
We were wrong.

00:06:16.530 --> 00:06:17.850
Good, good.

00:06:18.270 --> 00:06:20.200
Tsubaki-chan, can we go man—

00:06:20.200 --> 00:06:23.160
Can we go snake hunting?

00:06:26.000 --> 00:06:27.340
Go ahead.

00:06:29.240 --> 00:06:31.120
Hooray!

00:06:29.660 --> 00:06:31.120
Let's go, Asagao!

00:06:31.120 --> 00:06:32.620
Find that snake!

00:06:31.630 --> 00:06:32.620
Those two...

00:06:33.290 --> 00:06:35.360
Did they really learn their lesson?

00:06:35.860 --> 00:06:37.180
Want to go, too?

00:06:37.180 --> 00:06:38.450
Yes, let's.

00:06:39.400 --> 00:06:41.460
Oh, but before that...

00:06:42.140 --> 00:06:45.140
May I fix your mask string?

00:06:45.140 --> 00:06:47.300
Really? I'd love that!

00:06:51.970 --> 00:06:54.940
I appreciate it. I'm bad at that stuff.

00:06:54.940 --> 00:06:55.930
No problem.

00:06:55.930 --> 00:06:58.640
Those girls are such a handful, though.

00:06:58.870 --> 00:07:00.580
Calling snakes "men."

00:07:00.580 --> 00:07:01.480
Really.

00:07:07.360 --> 00:07:08.780
Um...

00:07:09.460 --> 00:07:13.580
Snakes and men aren't alike, right?

00:07:13.580 --> 00:07:14.200
Huh?

00:07:15.500 --> 00:07:19.040
Oh, that's right. 
You've never seen a man.

00:07:19.820 --> 00:07:21.290
They aren't alike at all.

00:07:21.770 --> 00:07:24.200
Men are people, just like us.

00:07:24.200 --> 00:07:25.250
Oh, yeah?!

00:07:25.250 --> 00:07:29.040
O-Okay, so what are the differences 
between men and women?

00:07:29.040 --> 00:07:32.930
Let's see... I think lots of 
men are taller than women.

00:07:32.930 --> 00:07:33.840
Really?!

00:07:33.840 --> 00:07:36.310
And they might have lots 
of hair on their bodies.

00:07:36.310 --> 00:07:38.220
Yeah?! Yeah?!

00:07:40.380 --> 00:07:43.100
You're curious about men, Tsubaki.

00:07:43.860 --> 00:07:46.450
O-Only a little bit, though.

00:07:47.160 --> 00:07:49.580
But never mind. Here, I'm done.

00:07:50.110 --> 00:07:51.410
That was quick.

00:07:51.410 --> 00:07:52.890
Try it on.

00:07:52.890 --> 00:07:53.530
Okay.

00:07:58.420 --> 00:08:00.880
Wow, it doesn't shift at all!

00:08:00.880 --> 00:08:01.960
Thanks.

00:08:01.960 --> 00:08:03.490
I'm glad it's better.

00:08:03.490 --> 00:08:06.410
Now, it's about time we hunted some snakes.

00:08:06.410 --> 00:08:07.070
Yeah.

00:08:10.510 --> 00:08:12.810
It's a relief, though.

00:08:13.240 --> 00:08:15.850
That men are people, too.

00:08:15.850 --> 00:08:17.780
And yet, the whole snake thing...

00:08:17.780 --> 00:08:19.210
Oh, but...

00:08:19.930 --> 00:08:22.140
Ding-a-lings are maybe a little like snakes.

00:08:22.140 --> 00:08:22.640
Eh?

00:08:23.180 --> 00:08:24.080
Ding...?

00:08:24.750 --> 00:08:33.700
Ding-a-ling! Ding-a-ling! Ding-a-ling! 
Ding-a-ling! Ding-a-ling!

00:08:34.860 --> 00:08:35.560
Huh?

00:08:37.250 --> 00:08:37.920
Huh?

00:08:38.460 --> 00:08:39.800
Nee-sama!

00:08:40.630 --> 00:08:42.270
Oh, Sazanka and Asagao.

00:08:42.270 --> 00:08:44.280
It went your way!

00:08:44.280 --> 00:08:45.170
There it is!

00:08:45.170 --> 00:08:46.380
Please catch it!

00:08:46.380 --> 00:08:47.690
I'll do it!

00:08:48.610 --> 00:08:51.350
I messed up before, but <i>this</i> time I'll—

00:08:55.030 --> 00:08:57.460
I tried... too hard.

00:08:58.020 --> 00:08:59.640
Rindou, you dummy!

00:08:59.910 --> 00:09:01.770
Tsubaki-chan! It's all you!

00:09:07.890 --> 00:09:11.650
<i>Men have something like 
that between their legs?</i>

00:09:11.650 --> 00:09:13.490
<b>Meat</b>

00:09:12.430 --> 00:09:13.490
<i>Between their legs...</i>

00:09:13.490 --> 00:09:15.330
<b>Meat</b>

00:09:14.050 --> 00:09:15.320
<i>This?!</i>

00:09:15.780 --> 00:09:17.660
<i>I feel so embarrassed!</i>

00:09:17.660 --> 00:09:18.930
Nee-sama!

00:09:19.690 --> 00:09:21.290
<i>I have to get a grip!</i>

00:09:21.970 --> 00:09:26.020
<i>That is a snake, not a man's...</i>

00:09:25.580 --> 00:09:26.670
<b>Meat</b>

00:09:26.020 --> 00:09:27.040
<i>Snake!</i>

00:09:26.670 --> 00:09:28.380
<b>Meat</b>

00:09:27.040 --> 00:09:28.380
<i>Right, a snake.</i>

00:09:29.140 --> 00:09:29.710
<i>Okay!</i>

00:09:30.050 --> 00:09:31.710
<i>Bring it on, sna—</i>

00:09:31.420 --> 00:09:34.710
Don't let that <i>man</i> get away!

00:09:35.210 --> 00:09:35.970
M—

00:09:42.460 --> 00:09:43.540
Stupid!

00:09:43.540 --> 00:09:44.270
Oh.

00:09:44.550 --> 00:09:48.700
I-I was wrong, Tsubaki-chan! 
I didn't mean to say "man."

00:09:48.700 --> 00:09:50.500
It just slipped out.

00:09:50.500 --> 00:09:53.130
That's not much of an excuse.

00:09:53.130 --> 00:09:54.740
U-Um...

00:09:59.840 --> 00:10:03.890
Her face is bright red! 
What now? She's super-pissed!

00:10:03.890 --> 00:10:06.290
I-It's your fault. Do something!

00:10:06.290 --> 00:10:08.060
Y-Yeah, but what?!

00:10:08.060 --> 00:10:09.880
Think of something yourself!

00:10:10.110 --> 00:10:11.630
Yes!

00:10:12.090 --> 00:10:14.300
I caught a man!

00:10:15.100 --> 00:10:17.150
Aww, lucky you.

00:10:20.500 --> 00:10:22.560
She's even angrier!

00:10:22.560 --> 00:10:24.620
What do we do?!

00:10:24.620 --> 00:10:26.580
Forgive me, Tsubaki-chan!

00:10:26.580 --> 00:10:29.100
Don't be angry, Nee-sama! 
I'm begging you!

00:10:29.100 --> 00:10:30.400
<i>I don't think...</i>

00:10:29.100 --> 00:10:30.400
We won't say "man" anymore!

00:10:30.720 --> 00:10:33.000
<i>...she's actually angry.</i>

00:10:35.280 --> 00:10:38.530
<b>What Defines Results</b>

00:10:37.190 --> 00:10:40.410
<b>Food</b>

00:10:37.190 --> 00:10:40.410
Let's see... This isn't it.

00:10:40.940 --> 00:10:45.430
Huh? That's weird. 
I thought I put it in here.

00:10:45.430 --> 00:10:48.170
Asagao, we need to hurry and go.

00:10:48.170 --> 00:10:50.080
Hold on!

00:10:50.380 --> 00:10:53.420
All the other teams have left already.

00:10:53.870 --> 00:10:56.590
I just need a little longer!

00:10:58.250 --> 00:10:59.820
Great...

00:10:59.820 --> 00:11:01.110
Hey, Tsubaki.

00:11:01.780 --> 00:11:05.760
I just realized... 
I've never seen Team Rooster.

00:11:05.760 --> 00:11:10.090
Oh, that's right. You have yet to meet them.

00:11:10.090 --> 00:11:12.110
Sorry for the delay!

00:11:14.830 --> 00:11:18.850
Team Rooster has been sequestered 
in the mountains for a while now.

00:11:18.850 --> 00:11:20.400
Oh, is that so?

00:11:20.400 --> 00:11:21.410
And so...

00:11:20.860 --> 00:11:23.440
Does that mean they're training?

00:11:21.410 --> 00:11:24.580
Hey, are you listening to me?

00:11:24.580 --> 00:11:25.800
I'm listening.

00:11:25.200 --> 00:11:28.660
I suppose it's for the sake of training.

00:11:25.800 --> 00:11:27.620
Hey, are you actually listening?

00:11:27.620 --> 00:11:28.660
I am, I am.

00:11:28.660 --> 00:11:29.200
Really?

00:11:29.200 --> 00:11:30.210
What is it already?

00:11:30.210 --> 00:11:31.650
Well, it's about the meat.

00:11:31.650 --> 00:11:33.150
Hey.

00:11:39.480 --> 00:11:40.480
Who're they?

00:11:41.500 --> 00:11:43.590
Are you from another village?

00:11:44.060 --> 00:11:45.530
Whoa, seriously?

00:11:45.530 --> 00:11:47.440
She hasn't picked up on it.

00:11:48.280 --> 00:11:49.960
Hey, you two.

00:11:50.980 --> 00:11:55.020
I know you haven't been to the village 
in a while, but don't be in such a hurry.

00:11:55.660 --> 00:11:56.770
Sumire!

00:11:56.770 --> 00:11:59.620
Hi. Been a long time, Tsubaki.

00:11:59.620 --> 00:12:00.980
That it has.

00:12:01.970 --> 00:12:03.440
Which means...

00:12:03.440 --> 00:12:04.690
These two...

00:12:05.070 --> 00:12:07.660
Yeah. They're Tanpopo and Azami.

00:12:07.660 --> 00:12:09.790
Huh?!

00:12:11.020 --> 00:12:12.910
By the way, who's that?

00:12:12.910 --> 00:12:14.310
This is Rindou.

00:12:14.310 --> 00:12:18.190
A new member of Team Dog, 
from another village.

00:12:18.190 --> 00:12:19.420
I see.

00:12:19.420 --> 00:12:21.350
I'm Sumire, leader of Team Rooster.

00:12:22.110 --> 00:12:23.750
N-Nice to meet you.

00:12:24.140 --> 00:12:26.460
You sure have changed, though.

00:12:26.460 --> 00:12:28.230
Don't stare like that.

00:12:28.230 --> 00:12:29.350
It's embarrassing.

00:12:29.350 --> 00:12:32.200
Those are the results of our mountain living.

00:12:32.200 --> 00:12:35.090
Seems like these two finally get it.

00:12:35.090 --> 00:12:36.230
Mhm.

00:12:36.230 --> 00:12:37.520
That's right.

00:12:38.340 --> 00:12:42.560
Next is... saying hello to Sensei.

00:12:39.730 --> 00:12:42.570
<b>•Breakfast
•Reach Akane Class

00:12:43.220 --> 00:12:46.690
I'll go do that briefly, so you 
two can stay here and chat.

00:12:46.690 --> 00:12:47.740
Yes, ma'am.

00:12:47.740 --> 00:12:49.340
We'll be waiting.

00:12:49.340 --> 00:12:51.030
Okay, see you.

00:12:57.830 --> 00:12:59.880
Are you really Tanpopo and Azami?

00:12:59.880 --> 00:13:02.210
I couldn't tell, at first.

00:13:03.510 --> 00:13:07.300
These two were undisciplined, 
so Sumire got mad,

00:13:07.300 --> 00:13:10.860
and took them up into the mountains 
to retrain their minds.

00:13:10.860 --> 00:13:11.800
Huh...

00:13:12.350 --> 00:13:14.940
What were you two like before?

00:13:17.180 --> 00:13:19.400
What were we like?

00:13:23.300 --> 00:13:25.600
We were like this!

00:13:25.600 --> 00:13:27.070
Yay!

00:13:27.870 --> 00:13:28.910
Say wha?

00:13:28.910 --> 00:13:32.640
Like, we'd totally had it with mountain life.

00:13:32.640 --> 00:13:34.820
It was fun for a while, y'know.

00:13:34.820 --> 00:13:36.490
Didn't have to go to class n'such.

00:13:36.730 --> 00:13:40.220
But y'know, you start 
missin' the village food!

00:13:40.220 --> 00:13:41.750
The village rules!

00:13:42.030 --> 00:13:45.490
And so, we pretended to 
be all reformed and junk.

00:13:45.490 --> 00:13:48.240
And we fooled Sumire-chi.

00:13:48.240 --> 00:13:49.670
Now we're home!

00:13:49.670 --> 00:13:51.290
Yay!

00:13:55.600 --> 00:13:58.010
Well, I figured it was something like that.

00:13:58.740 --> 00:14:01.480
Good ol' Sazanka, sharp as a tack!

00:14:01.480 --> 00:14:05.680
Hey. That mask is the cutest, Rindo-chi.

00:14:05.680 --> 00:14:06.950
Th-Thanks.

00:14:06.950 --> 00:14:08.330
Check it out!

00:14:08.330 --> 00:14:12.440
We brought back a super extra-large 
boatload of souvenirs.

00:14:12.860 --> 00:14:16.150
We've just <i>got</i> to celebrate our return!

00:14:16.150 --> 00:14:17.570
Yay!

00:14:17.570 --> 00:14:18.700
Whoo!

00:14:19.180 --> 00:14:22.660
Whoo, whoo, whoo-whoo!

00:14:27.470 --> 00:14:29.210
This's good!

00:14:29.530 --> 00:14:32.550
Hey, won't there be trouble 
if Sumire finds out?

00:14:32.550 --> 00:14:35.800
No worries. She won't be back for a while.

00:14:36.070 --> 00:14:39.240
She was sayin' she had a 
ton of stuff to report.

00:14:39.240 --> 00:14:43.700
Sumire-chi is sooo serious, 
she does everything according to a plan.

00:14:43.700 --> 00:14:45.010
Sure does!

00:14:46.020 --> 00:14:49.370
Things must be difficult for serious Sumire.

00:14:49.370 --> 00:14:51.770
These two are kind of amazing.

00:14:58.570 --> 00:15:00.630
<i>There's some presence.</i>

00:15:02.940 --> 00:15:06.140
Won't we be back in the hills 
if she <i>does</i> find out?

00:15:08.610 --> 00:15:09.980
That's the ticket.

00:15:09.980 --> 00:15:11.980
What a kicker that would be.

00:15:11.980 --> 00:15:13.610
Totes bad news.

00:15:18.060 --> 00:15:19.430
<i>She's here!</i>

00:15:19.740 --> 00:15:22.810
<i>Sumire's ninjutsu specialty, Invisibility!</i>

00:15:23.080 --> 00:15:25.100
Well, she'll never find out.

00:15:26.500 --> 00:15:27.680
You said it!

00:15:27.680 --> 00:15:28.820
What a laugh!

00:15:28.820 --> 00:15:29.440
Well said!

00:15:30.020 --> 00:15:32.690
<i>Sh-She knows all about it, you two!</i>

00:15:34.590 --> 00:15:36.530
<i>I figured it was something like this.</i>

00:15:36.530 --> 00:15:37.040
<b>•Breakfast
•Reach Akane Class
•
•Greet Sensei</b>

00:15:37.040 --> 00:15:41.000
<b>•Breakfast
•Reach Akane Class
•Final confirmation
•Greet Sensei</b>

00:15:37.390 --> 00:15:40.990
<i>They thought I'd stick to the 
plan, so they got careless.</i>

00:15:40.990 --> 00:15:44.200
But y'know, Sumire-chi is so totally uptight.

00:15:45.040 --> 00:15:47.620
She'd do better to go more with the flow.

00:15:47.620 --> 00:15:49.460
I so get that!

00:15:49.460 --> 00:15:51.560
Aren't there times when 
she's stiff as a statue?

00:15:50.760 --> 00:15:55.050
<i>Uh-oh! I bet she's planning 
some kind of punishment!</i>

00:15:51.560 --> 00:15:53.850
Oh, yeah. All the time!

00:15:55.300 --> 00:15:59.890
H-Hey! Sumire might come back 
anytime, so we should—

00:15:59.890 --> 00:16:01.240
We'll be fine.

00:16:01.240 --> 00:16:04.560
She's so serious, I'm sure she's 
takin' her time with hellos.

00:16:06.820 --> 00:16:08.740
I have just returned home.

00:16:08.740 --> 00:16:11.180
She'd do that! Too funny!

00:16:14.000 --> 00:16:17.230
Sumire-chi's also way strict with training.

00:16:17.230 --> 00:16:19.240
Waterfall training's cold!

00:16:19.620 --> 00:16:22.700
It really was no joke. 
She was such a witch then.

00:16:23.790 --> 00:16:26.720
And Sumire-chi's cooking is super yuck.

00:16:26.720 --> 00:16:29.420
Oh, that Chinese herb stuff, or whatever?

00:16:29.420 --> 00:16:32.340
Yeah, that. No more for me, thanks.

00:16:31.650 --> 00:16:33.300
<i>They really are...</i>

00:16:32.340 --> 00:16:35.300
What is it? Medicine? It stinks.

00:16:33.300 --> 00:16:37.050
<i>They're going to get some 
serious rehabilitation!</i>

00:16:35.300 --> 00:16:37.050
It does. I bet it's not even food.

00:16:37.050 --> 00:16:42.520
<b>•Breakfast
•Reach Akane Class
•Final confirmation
•Greet Sensei
•MOUNTAIN TRAINING
•Waterfall training •Chopping firewood
•Lockstep from hell
•Shuriken throwing •Jump-roping
•Endless Koppo •Torture
•Rope-tying •Fasting
•Turtle Walking to the limit</b>

00:16:37.730 --> 00:16:39.860
<i>It'll be the deluxe mountain training course!</i>

00:16:44.450 --> 00:16:47.610
<i>They really can't stand me, though.</i>

00:16:48.440 --> 00:16:53.620
<i>But of course, to them, 
I'm a nagging upperclassman.</i>

00:16:54.620 --> 00:16:57.280
<i>But that has nothing to do with this.</i>

00:16:57.690 --> 00:17:01.740
<i>I will do what I must, 
as the leader of Team Rooster!</i>

00:17:04.520 --> 00:17:06.660
H-Hey, how about her good points?

00:17:07.070 --> 00:17:07.950
Huh?

00:17:07.950 --> 00:17:12.040
Could you two tell us what you 
think are Sumire's good points?

00:17:12.320 --> 00:17:14.660
Sumire-chi's good points?

00:17:23.060 --> 00:17:24.640
<i>I guess there aren't any.</i>

00:17:25.480 --> 00:17:27.400
<i>What am I doing, getting my hopes up?</i>

00:17:27.400 --> 00:17:28.670
Okay...

00:17:30.160 --> 00:17:31.400
You wanna know?

00:17:33.410 --> 00:17:35.320
Yes, by all means!

00:17:35.580 --> 00:17:37.400
First off, she's kind!

00:17:37.680 --> 00:17:42.030
Yeah! She goes and gets things 
ready for training and such.

00:17:42.030 --> 00:17:44.970
If you have a fever, she's super devoted!

00:17:44.970 --> 00:17:46.620
And she wipes away your sweat.

00:17:46.620 --> 00:17:49.470
She's not choosy, either. 
Talk about great!

00:17:49.470 --> 00:17:51.600
Also, she's cute, yeah?

00:17:51.600 --> 00:17:52.950
Yeah, she's cute.

00:17:52.950 --> 00:17:54.960
And reliable, in her own way.

00:17:54.960 --> 00:17:58.830
And when she gets mad, 
isn't it for our own good?

00:17:58.830 --> 00:18:00.730
It sure is!

00:18:00.730 --> 00:18:03.970
Isn't that the best, being cute and reliable?

00:18:03.970 --> 00:18:07.170
The best! Sumire-chi's super cool!

00:18:07.170 --> 00:18:10.230
You two like Sumire-chan, don't you?

00:18:11.500 --> 00:18:13.440
Huh? What're you sayin'?

00:18:13.720 --> 00:18:15.840
Did you seriously say that?

00:18:17.870 --> 00:18:19.680
We love her!

00:18:20.370 --> 00:18:22.610
And we totally respect her!

00:18:24.410 --> 00:18:27.910
Also, also, Sumire-chi may not look it, but—

00:18:33.460 --> 00:18:35.090
Hi, girls.

00:18:35.090 --> 00:18:36.300
Huh?!

00:18:36.300 --> 00:18:38.240
Sumire-chi! Why're you here?!

00:18:38.240 --> 00:18:41.320
Have you been listening in?! 
That's not fair, y'know!

00:18:42.210 --> 00:18:44.590
This is, you know, one of them things.

00:18:44.590 --> 00:18:48.550
We were just showin' 
Rindou how we used to be.

00:18:48.550 --> 00:18:51.340
I heard it all, from the start.

00:18:52.390 --> 00:18:55.810
Sumire-chi, no more mountain training. Cool?

00:18:55.810 --> 00:18:58.020
It's out of style these days.

00:18:58.020 --> 00:19:01.470
Say what you like, but I'm team leader.

00:19:01.470 --> 00:19:04.360
The schedule is the schedule. 
You're going to stick to it.

00:19:05.270 --> 00:19:07.080
And so, first...

00:19:09.360 --> 00:19:13.200
You two will say hello to Sensei, 
then eat, and take a bath.

00:19:14.730 --> 00:19:15.410
Right?

00:19:17.260 --> 00:19:19.220
<b>•Bath
•Food</b>

00:19:22.090 --> 00:19:23.160
Come on, let's go.

00:19:27.370 --> 00:19:29.420
Sumire-chi...

00:19:30.830 --> 00:19:33.520
It's super creepy when you're too kind.

00:19:33.520 --> 00:19:35.440
Yeah. It's kinda scary.

00:19:35.700 --> 00:19:37.650
Or even horrifying.

00:19:38.000 --> 00:19:40.110
Not your thing.

00:19:42.220 --> 00:19:45.380
You'll eat, take a bath, 
then back into the mountains!

00:19:45.380 --> 00:19:46.780
Anything but that!

00:19:46.780 --> 00:19:49.100
Although that sounds more 
like you, Sumire-chi!

00:19:49.100 --> 00:19:50.390
Then, you'll have no objections.

00:19:49.740 --> 00:19:52.630
Must be hard, being on Team Rooster.

00:19:50.390 --> 00:19:54.260
No, wrong! Those're two different things!

00:19:54.260 --> 00:19:55.630
I'd say so.

00:21:31.900 --> 00:21:34.300
I'm totally wiped again today.

00:21:34.300 --> 00:21:38.000
"Totally" is right. 
Sumire-chi's training is too hard.

00:21:38.000 --> 00:21:39.700
And her lectures are too long.

00:21:39.700 --> 00:21:41.530
She'll all relentless and junk.

00:21:41.530 --> 00:21:45.420
Too true. Like, demon lord level ruthless.

00:21:45.420 --> 00:21:50.160
But now and then, she'll flip and 
turn into Princess Forehead Veins.

00:21:50.160 --> 00:21:52.000
I know, right?

00:21:52.000 --> 00:21:55.330
In fact, when that happens, 
<i>I</i> get all worried about <i>her</i>.

00:21:55.330 --> 00:21:59.900
I so get that. 
Makes me worry just thinkin' about it.

00:21:59.900 --> 00:22:03.970
And that thing today wasn't right! 
<i>So</i> not fair!

00:22:03.970 --> 00:22:06.150
That one thing, right? Lockstep...

00:22:06.150 --> 00:22:08.240
Lockstep from hell.

00:22:08.240 --> 00:22:10.180
Totally don't get it.

00:22:10.180 --> 00:22:13.080
She made us walk so much, my legs are done.

00:22:13.080 --> 00:22:15.460
My legs are DOA, too.

00:22:15.460 --> 00:22:20.190
And hey, doesn't the name of Sumire-chi's 
crash course program totally suck?

00:22:20.190 --> 00:22:21.710
For real, though.

00:22:21.710 --> 00:22:24.300
What was it again? Turtle Walk...

00:22:24.300 --> 00:22:25.970
Turtle Walk to the limit!

00:22:25.970 --> 00:22:27.120
That one!

00:22:27.120 --> 00:22:29.280
No flair!

00:22:29.280 --> 00:22:31.510
I totally broke a nail on that one.

00:22:31.510 --> 00:22:34.380
I saw, I so saw. You totally did!

00:22:34.380 --> 00:22:35.790
Sucks.

00:22:35.790 --> 00:22:39.220
Sucks to the max, downer-towner.

00:22:39.220 --> 00:22:40.530
Hey, check this out.

00:22:40.530 --> 00:22:43.470
I got so bored, so I totally decked it. 
Isn't it adorbs?

00:22:43.470 --> 00:22:46.460
Ooh, noice! It's cute but powerful.

00:22:46.460 --> 00:22:50.240
But if Sumire-chi finds it, 
she might go witch-mode again.

00:22:50.240 --> 00:22:55.260
She could. But if we don't do this stuff, 
mountain life'd be the pits.

00:22:55.260 --> 00:22:59.180
That's true. It'll get worse than 
we can bear—off the charts.

00:22:59.180 --> 00:23:02.100
For that matter, don't you worry 
the mighty golden age of our youth

00:23:02.100 --> 00:23:05.270
could just fade away up here 
in the mountains like this?

00:23:07.300 --> 00:23:09.980
Hold on! That'll never happen!

00:23:09.980 --> 00:23:10.590
Huh?

00:23:10.590 --> 00:23:12.750
As long our Team Rooster 
trio has each other,

00:23:12.750 --> 00:23:15.770
we'll just have to live it up, 
even up here in the deserted mountains!

00:23:15.770 --> 00:23:17.940
Spread our wings and fly!

00:23:17.940 --> 00:23:20.560
I'll say! We've already got it made!

00:23:21.120 --> 00:23:25.550
Team Rooster! BFFs for life! 
Forever indestructible!

00:23:25.550 --> 00:23:29.180
Sumire-chi'll be back in 
a jiff, but before that!

00:23:29.180 --> 00:23:30.900
Might as well dance?

00:23:30.900 --> 00:23:32.550
Yay!

00:23:36.970 --> 00:23:39.980
<b>Next time:

00:23:37.260 --> 00:23:39.010
To be continued!
